  "training_rule": "Freeze all pose models, the obstruction-weighted base metric head, and the tail-risk head. Fit one three-parameter linear scaler from only the frozen base metric and tail-risk score. Map its scalar through a multiplier constrained to [0.5,2.0], then clamp the corrected metric to [0.25,10.0] mm. Train for exactly 50 epochs at quantile 0.975 with weights equal to 0.75 marginal unit weight plus 0.25 mean-normalized obstruction weight. Normalize only from 79M. The training-only risk CDF is used only for a selection utility proxy. No selection-based stopping, feature, architecture, objective-balance, multiplier-range, quantile, or threshold sweep.",
  "selection_rule": "Apply once on untouched 80M scenes. Require all prior metric gates with scene AUROC >=0.72 and every condition image AUROC >=0.70. Require mean pinball loss no worse than the frozen base head, median bound <=1.10 times the base, and noninferior partial/full coverage. For a development-only utility proxy, count images with corrected metric <=1.8 mm and training-CDF risk percentile <=0.40; require >=0.08 overall, >=0.02 absolute improvement over the base, and condition fractions >=0.05/0.08/0.02/0.015. Passing selects only a compact research correction for new mapping calibration and selection; it installs no qualification or runtime authority.",
